// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_lnx_chroot_execution.yml
// ID Sigma: f2bed782-994e-4f40-9cd5-518198cb3fba
// Título: Linux Sudo Chroot Execution
// Descripción: Detects the execution of 'sudo' command with '--chroot' option, which is used to change the root directory for command execution.
Attackers may use this technique to evade detection and execute commands in a modified environment.
This can be part of a privilege escalation strategy, as it allows the execution of commands with elevated privileges in a controlled environment as seen in CVE-2025-32463.
While investigating, look out for unusual or unexpected use of 'sudo --chroot' in conjunction with other commands or scripts such as execution from temporary directories or unusual user accounts.

// Fecha de creación: 2025-10-02
// Fecha de modificación: 
// Aplica a: Producto: linux | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: linux
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: low
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\linux\process_creation\proc_creation_lnx_chroot_execution.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/sudo" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " --chroot " or ProcessCommandLine contains "sudo -R ")
